---
description: Transfile stack, security, and UI rules
alwaysApply: true
---
Project: Transfile, a file sharing app with folders, passwords and expiry.

Structure: apps/web (React+Vite), apps/api (Hono on Workers),
packages/shared (Zod schemas/types).

Rules:
- TypeScript strict. No `any`.
- Validate ALL request input with Zod schemas from packages/shared.
- All DB access via Drizzle. Never build SQL from user input.
- Every route touching a file/folder/share MUST verify the user owns it.
- Never trust client-reported file sizes: verify against R2 after upload.
- Hash passwords with Web Crypto (PBKDF2). Free Worker CPU limit is ~10ms.
- Uploads/downloads use presigned R2 URLs, never streamed through the Worker.
- Read SPEC.md before implementing. One feature per session.

UI:
- shadcn/ui + Tailwind only. Restyle base components once in components/ui.
- Rounded-3xl cards, rounded-full buttons, soft gray surfaces on white,
  soft shadows, minimal borders. Dark primary button, blue accent, green for
  success/progress. No glows, gradient borders or decorative animation.
- Use theme tokens, never ad-hoc colours or radii.
- Motion only for functional transitions.
- Mobile-first: Drawer on mobile, Dialog on desktop.
- Reference designs are in /docs/ui-references.
